          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon  X \to Y
            between categories one may ask for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon  y_1 \to y_2
            that, if given a lift of its target
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \hat y_2
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^p
                  \\\
                  Y &amp;&amp;&amp; y_1 &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; y_2
                  }
          %p
            there be a
            %em universal
            lift of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp;&amp; \hat y_1 &amp;\stackrel{\hat f}{\to}&amp; \hat y_2
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^p
                  \\\
                  Y &amp;&amp;&amp; y_1 &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; y_2
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            There may also be other lifts of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is essentially uniquely determined by its target
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat y_2
            and its image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = p(\hat f)
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "." do
              %strong cartesian morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{op}\colon X^{op}\to Y^{op}
            is called
            %strong opcartesian
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong cocartesian
          %p
            If there are enough cartesian morphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^* : X_{y_2} \to X_{y_1}
          %p
            between the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_1
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_2
          %p
            This way a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
            with enough Cartesian morphisms – called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration"} Cartesian fibration
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            – determines and is determined by a fiber-assigning functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to Cat^{op}
          %p
            This has its analog in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_categories In categories
          %h4#traditional_definition Traditional definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (cartesian morphism)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x_1 \to x_2
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %strong strongly cartesian
              with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              (nowadays often just
              = succeed ")," do
                %em cartesian
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-cartesian
              if for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x'\in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:x'\to x_2
              and every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo :
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u:p(x')\to p(x_1)
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(h) = p(f) u
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v:x'\to x_1
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h = f v
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = p(v)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∀
                            %mi x
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mo !
                                  %mi v
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∀
                                  %mi h
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∀
                                  %mi u
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\forall x'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\exists! v}} &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\forall h}}
                    \\\
                    x_1 &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; x_2
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\stackrel{p}{\mapsto}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    p(x')
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\forall u}} &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{p(h)}}
                    \\\
                    p(x_1) &amp;\stackrel{p(f)}{\to}&amp; p(x_2)
                    }
            %p
              In imprecise words: for all commuting triangles in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              (involving
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(f)
              as above) and all lifts through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              of its 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (involving
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as above), there is a unique refinement to a lift of the entire commuting triangle.
            %p
              We can make this definition slightly more explicit by working with the fibres of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
