            %p
              If we pass to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(Y)
              of the categories, then in terms of diagrams in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              this means that the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
              is
              = succeed "-cartesian" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              inclusions
