            %p
              The bottom-right square and wide rectangle are pullbacks by construction. By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
              = succeed "-cartesian," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{/f} \to X_{/x}
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{/f} \to X_{/x}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! : X_{/x} \to X_{/y}
          %p
            To make this concrete, we can also discuss adaptations of the abstract idea to two different models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            theory:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+categories"} sSet categories
          %h4#in_quasicategories In quasi-categories
          %p
            We formulate a notion
            %strong cartesian edge
            or
            %em cartesian morphism
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            relative to a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
            of simplicial sets. In the case that these simplicial sets are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-categories
            – i.e. simplicial set incarnations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            – this yields a notion of cartesian morphisms in
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
            be a morphism of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x_1 \to x_2
            be an edge in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Delta^1 \to X
          %p
            Recall the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over quasi-category
            obtained from the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+quasi-categories"} join of quasi-categories
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/f
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/{x_2}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/p(f)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/p(x_2)
            in generalization of the categories considered in the above definition of cartesian morphisms in categories.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (cartesian edge in a simplicial set)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+Kan+fibration"} inner Kan fibration
              of simplicial sets.
            %p
              Then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-cartesian
              if the induced morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
